From 83095fb81e3f0f477c1186826c5a1b7e1d854138 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:22:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Expo SDK 54: React Native 0.81, React 19 (Q-019)

Both stores now refuse SDK 52. App Store uploads need Xcode 26 since
28 April 2026, which Expo supports from SDK 54, and new Play apps must
target Android API 36 since 31 August 2026. This is Q-019, the one
before-launch item the review could do itself once launch became the
store apps.

- expo 52 to 54, with every Expo module at the version SDK 54 expects
  (`expo install --check` clean): react-native 0.81.5, react and
  react-dom 19.1.0, react-native-web 0.21, reanimated 4.1 (its
  worklets now in react-native-worklets, so babel names that plugin),
  gesture-handler 2.28, screens 4.16, safe-area-context 5.6, svg
  15.12, async-storage 2.2.
- nativewind 4.2.7 and react-native-css-interop 0.2.7, the first to
  support Reanimated 4.
- React 19's types: @types/react 19.1, react-test-renderer 19.1, and
  `JSX` imported from react where the global namespace was used.
- babel-preset-expo is no longer reached through expo, so it is a dev
  dependency, pinned to the 54 line Expo itself names (~54.0.12).
  `expo install` offered 58, for a later SDK, because its version list
  could not be fetched here.

expo-av stays: SDK 54 still ships it (16.0), and SDK 55 removes it.
Moving to expo-audio is recorded for that upgrade. The package.json
description's dash was rewritten from an escape to the character by
expo install. No native build was made here (Q-001 needs the
developer accounts).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FgFsmHsJ32w9Di1MVKqKTX
